  "facts": [
    "The Woronora River Bridge, completed in 2001, was the largest incrementally launched bridge in the Southern Hemisphere, featuring both horizontal and vertical curves.",
    "Designed to replace a steep, hairpin-laden route, the bridge eliminated the old two-lane low-level bridge opened in 1981, which itself replaced a 1912 single-lane timber span.",
    "With a 4.7% downhill grade at the launching abutment, the bridge earned the Australian Construction Achievement Award in 2002 for its record‑setting steep launch."
